<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka May '97 tea production up 6.7 percent.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka May '97 tea production up 6.7 percent.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's black tea production in May this year rose by nearly seven percent to 27.37 million kg against 25.65 million kg in the same month in 1996, the Sri Lanka Tea Board said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>But total production in the first five months of 1997 fell five percent to 103.5 million kg against 109 million in the same period last year, the Tea Board said.</p>
<p>The statement did not give any reasons for the overall fall in production this year.</p>
</text>
